PRETABLE -- #529 kill table 4 (TARGETED), written BEFORE the table (mtime is the order proof)
Instrument: regress/crime_width_probe.py after the CLOSING-PASS repair, frozen by the driver as crime_width_probe.table4.py
-- 111 rows emitted (77 row() call sites by the ast deriver; table 3: 56 sites / 85 rows).  First measurements (L1):
../probe_first5_fix.out 110/110 on the FIXED build (repair 4, 76 sites), every new row as intended.  Then, while writing
THIS block, I found repair 4's `top4 anchor' could not see the Opus seat's acc4_210: that mutant refuses the 4R at
+0x210 (the slot's HIGH half, which answers 0 accepted or refused -- the prelude rewrites the slot on every access), and
the row reads +0x214.  The Opus seat's own discriminator was the NOTICE ("lw +0x210: notices 0 -> 1, value 0 both"), so
the repair (5) adds `lw +0x210' to the top session and a row `top said' = the session's one refusal (lb +0x27b) still
announces -- i.e. every accept cell touched before it was accepted.  Re-measured in ../probe_first6_fix.out before this
table (the driver's BASE run is the second measurement).

WHAT CHANGED SINCE TABLE 3, and the finding that bought each (closing pass: panel_20260913_110853 + the Opus closing seat)
  acc8 near (ld +0x00 -> 0x11)       the 8-byte window's NEAR end is +0x00, not +0x30 (grok: near8)
  sb08 +sb 0xff; sh08b +0x0900,+0xffff; IRQ and TIME refused stores now 0xff / 0xffff
                                     a CONTROL fall-through keyed on an untested data bit (kimi CLI: c_bit1), ENDIANESS
                                     never written set (glm: c_endian), a nonzero-write fall-through (Opus: wnz_lbl)
  sh08b once, rev once, imask/istat once, time once, dog once, hi once
                                     a latch keyed on the label (glm: lt_ctl), on a range (kimi-k3:cloud: lt_rng), on the
                                     block (Opus: lt_blk), on direction x width (Opus: lt_wl)
  rev v0 x2, imask/istat lb/lh v0, time lb/lh v0, dog v0, ctl v0, top rd v0
                                     the ANSWER at a named label (codex: rev_od1 / istat_od1 / time_od1) and in the far
                                     block (Opus: rd_hi)
  rearm session (14 accepted kinds)  a re-arm in the 4-byte arm (codex + Opus: rearm4), at a switch arm (Opus: rearm_time)
  latch x5 prologue (sw 0x01 +0x08, sw/lw +0x34)
                                     a pre-set by a 4-byte access (Opus: pre4), a second latch reusing bit 0 (ctl_collide)
  gate session (HARDINT via MACE, line asserted, refused sh 0x0800)
                                     the decline gated on HARDINT / prev_asserted (Opus: hi_gate, pa_gate)
  hi: + refused sh +0x27c 0xffff     a 2-byte store landing >= 0x200 (Opus: wst_mc2)
  top: + lw +0x214, lw +0x210, lb +0x27b, top said
                                     4-byte accept narrowed at the anchor's slot (Opus: acc4_210)
  TIME comment corrected (Opus: the first tick fires after the first ld); the "66-132" disclosure figure -> 66-990

WARRANT FOR TARGETING.  Sessions UNCHANGED since table 3 (same command list, rows unchanged): rev pc ctl, sw08 halts,
sw08 msg ctl, the +0x30 accept session, the six refused-width sessions, sh08, lh rev (one `print' added), sb/sh rev, keeps,
free.  CHANGED: controls, sb08, sh08b, lb rev, imask, istat, TIME x4, top, hi, latch x5; NEW: gate, rearm, dog.
  RULE: an earlier kill is RE-RUN iff EVERY row it reddened sits in a changed session -- then its detection is actually
  at stake.  A kill with at least one red row in an unchanged session stands (its row, its session and the binary are
  unchanged; the new rows can only add reds).  By that rule, from tables 1-3:
    len2only (t1: sb08 msg, lb rev pc)  acc8dog  acc4low  annlow  timeft  imaskft  a_istat  l_addrmask  x_mc4  x_mc8
    istat2  imask2  time2  istatsh  remap  h_imask  h_lbl  lt_len  lt_addr  wst_mc  c_dog  c_hrclr
  plus dogft and ctlrdft -- EQUIVALENTS, re-measured because the new `dog v0' and `ctl v0' rows read exactly their cells.
  STANDING on an unchanged-session row: revert fault exit0 fallsw len1only readonly wronly nolatch latchinv fmtswap acc8w
  acc8r acc4wlo acc4whi acc4rlo acc4rhi revwrite addrrc mmreads fdebug wstore only1r only2r only1w only2w a_lo10
  l_noonce static_od rearm lt_wset.  NOT re-run, dispositions unchanged: return1 (equivalent; its warrant, memory_rw's
  #95 pre-zero and the tail's identities, is untouched by an instrument change), acc8mid, sft, wstore31 (disclosed; no
  new row touches +0x100, +0x20 or +0x31).
  The Opus closing seat's o_lt_len and o_c_dog are BYTE-IDENTICAL mutants to table 3's lt_len and c_dog (checked by
  applying both): run once, as lt_len and c_dog.

TWO PROBE LANES -- why that is safe for THIS instrument, stated rather than assumed.  Every oracle but the TIME rows is
counted in guest STEPS (a tick fires on a step count, not a wall clock; the IRQ rows' tick assumption is step-counted);
the TIME rows compare s1 (66-990 measured, across 52 cells) and s2 (~2.8e8) against SMALL = 6.6e6 -- four orders of
magnitude each way.  Builds stay serial in one clone.  Any red row OUTSIDE its prediction is re-run alone before it is
believed.

CHANNEL -- per mutant, the rows PREDICTED to red on the 111-row instrument (CONTROL=OK unless said)
  base          none (111/111)
  len2only      lb nodflt, sb nodflt, sb08 msg (2: sb 0x01 and 0xff both print), lb rev pc, sb rev pc, imask lb/sb/lh/sh,
                istat lb/sb/lh/sh (a 1-byte fall-through at cause 1 sets IP2 and it is STICKY), time lb, time sb,
                hi nodflt  -- 16, 95/111.  (Its table-1 red set pre-dates the nodflt rows; lb/sb nodflt are the
                unchanged-session reds it now also has.)
  acc8dog       acc8 near, gate hardint, gate line (sd INTMASK refused, ld HARDINT answers 0), imask ctl, istat ctl,
                time lb/sb/lh/sh ctl (every ld refused: s2 = 0), top8 anchor, top said (ld +0x210 takes the notice),
                top8 st+ld, top4 rhi, top4 rlo, top4 w  -- 15, 96/111, CONTROL=FAIL.  hi keeps GREEN (its ld is refused,
                answers 0 = the want); imask/istat/time `once' GREEN (the notice is the refused sd's or ld's, one)
  acc4low       top4 anchor, top said, top4 rhi, top4 rlo, top4 w  -- 106/111
  annlow        hi said, top said (a refusal >= 0x40 prints nothing; hi once stays 1 -- lb +0x07 announces)  -- 109/111
  timeft        time lb, time sb, time lh, time sh  -- 107/111
  imaskft       imask lb, sb, lh, sh (sticky IP2)  -- 107/111
  a_istat       istat lb, sb, lh, sh  -- 107/111
  l_addrmask    hi said, top said (the text says 0x3f / 0x3b)  -- 109/111
  x_mc4         top4 anchor, top said, top4 rhi, top4 rlo, top4 w  -- 106/111
  x_mc8         top8 anchor, top said, top8 st+ld, top4 rhi, top4 rlo, top4 w  -- 105/111; hi keeps GREEN (ld refused -> 0)
  dogft         none -- EQUIVALENT (the DOG arm is `break;': dog v0 reads the tail's 0)  111/111
  ctlrdft       none -- EQUIVALENT (CONTROL acts only on writes: ctl v0 reads the tail's 0)  111/111
  istat2        istat lh, istat sh  -- 109/111
  imask2        imask lh, imask sh  -- 109/111
  time2         time lh, time sh  -- 109/111
  istatsh       istat sh  -- 110/111
  remap         top8 anchor, top4 anchor (both read reg[2] = INTSTAT = 0)  -- 109/111; the +0x278 round trips land on
                reg[7], TIME's slot, and also red only IF a later tick adds to TIME inside the session (not predicted)
  h_imask       imask lh, imask sh  -- 109/111
  h_lbl         imask lh/sh, istat lh/sh, time lh/sh  -- 105/111
  lt_len        latch x5 (lh first leaves bit 0 clear: 2), sh08b once (four 2-byte refusals: 4)  -- 109/111
  lt_addr       latch x5, sh08b once, imask once, istat once, rev once, time once, dog once (every session whose first
                refusal is at an EVEN address and is followed by an odd one or another even one)  -- 104/111
  wst_mc        hi keeps (0xffff: the sh +0x27c lands last)  -- 110/111
  c_dog         sh08b msg (0x0201 falls in, bit 0 prints), sh08b run (0x0a00 falls in and stops the CPUs)  -- 109/111
  c_hrclr       sb08 msg, sh08b msg  -- 109/111
  o_rearm4      rearm once (10: the nine accepted 4-byte kinds each re-arm)  -- 110/111
  o_pre4        latch x5 (0 notices: the prologue's 4-byte accesses pre-set), top said (lw +0x214 pre-sets)  -- 109/111
